§§ `s 37 -- maintenance and the age of 18`

-- A child born 10 May 2009, damages held on trust under a court order of 1 June 2020; vested interest, no contrary
-- intention. Arguments (1)(a): birth, today, interest continues, instrument date, contingent, carries income, contrary.
#ASSERT `May my trustee use the income for me while I am under 18` (`d` 10 5 2009) (`d` 9 5 2027) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May my trustee use the income for me while I am under 18` (`d` 10 5 2009) (`d` 10 5 2027) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May my trustee use the income for me while I am under 18` (`d` 10 5 2009) (`d` 1 1 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May my trustee use the income for me while I am under 18` (`d` 10 5 2009) (`d` 1 1 2026) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2020) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May my trustee use the income for me while I am under 18` (`d` 10 5 2009) (`d` 1 1 2026) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2020) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May my trustee use the income for me while I am under 18` (`d` 10 5 2009) (`d` 1 1 2026) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 37(5): a will of a testator who died 31 March 1959 (before 1 April 1959): s 37 does not apply; 1 April 1959: it does.
#ASSERT `May my trustee use the income for me while I am under 18` (`d` 10 5 2009) (`d` 1 1 2026) TRUE (`d` 31 3 1959) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May my trustee use the income for me while I am under 18` (`d` 10 5 2009) (`d` 1 1 2026) TRUE (`d` 1 4 1959) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- (1)(b). Arguments: birth, today, vested in income, failed, instrument date, contingent, carries income, contrary.
-- Contingent on reaching 25, carrying the income.
#ASSERT `Must my trustee pay me the income now I am 18` (`d` 10 5 2009) (`d` 10 5 2027) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 6 2020) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must my trustee pay me the income now I am 18` (`d` 10 5 2009) (`d` 9 5 2027) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 6 2020) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must my trustee pay me the income now I am 18` (`d` 10 5 2009) (`d` 10 5 2027) TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 6 2020) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must my trustee pay me the income now I am 18` (`d` 10 5 2009) (`d` 10 5 2027) FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 6 2020) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must my trustee pay me the income now I am 18` (`d` 10 5 2009) (`d` 10 5 2027) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 6 2020) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (2). Arguments: birth, today, married under 18, vested in income, entitled to property, instrument date, contingent,
-- carries income, contrary.
#ASSERT `What happens to the income saved for me while under 18` (`d` 10 5 2009) (`d` 1 1 2026) FALSE TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `they are still being accumulated, and the trustees may apply them as income meanwhile`
#ASSERT `What happens to the income saved for me while under 18` (`d` 10 5 2009) (`d` 10 5 2027) FALSE TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `they are held in trust for me absolutely`
#ASSERT `What happens to the income saved for me while under 18` (`d` 10 5 2009) (`d` 10 5 2027) FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 6 2020) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `they are held in trust for me absolutely`
#ASSERT `What happens to the income saved for me while under 18` (`d` 10 5 2009) (`d` 10 5 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 6 2020) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `they are added to the capital of the property`
#ASSERT `What happens to the income saved for me while under 18` (`d` 10 5 2009) (`d` 1 1 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `they are held in trust for me absolutely`
#ASSERT `What happens to the income saved for me while under 18` (`d` 10 5 2009) (`d` 10 5 2027) FALSE TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

